{#-
  One page per GROUP rather than per case, because the four cases in a
  group answer one reader's question from four angles and a page each
  would be four pages of preamble. Every case keeps its own transcript
  (typed, like the home page's), what it reads, and the steps that set
  it up as buttons that go somewhere real.

  The rail lists all eleven cases under their three headings and marks
  the group you are in; each case is an anchor on its group's page.

  The transcript is the site's signature element and its whole job is to
  be concrete: a real question, a real answer, and a citation under the
  answer saying what was read to produce it. Every tool named under a
  window is in the registry — the build links each one to its own
  heading in the tool reference, and a name the registry does not know
  fails the site's tests.
-#}
<div class="siterail">
  <nav class="siterail__nav" aria-label="Use cases">
    {%- for g in usecases %}
    <div class="rail__group">{{ g.group }}</div>
    {%- for c in g.cases %}
    <a class="rail__item{% if g.group == group.group %} rail__item--on{% endif %}" href="/use-cases/{{ g.cases[0].key }}#{{ c.key }}"{% if g.group == group.group and loop.first %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ c.label }}</a>
    {%- endfor %}
    {%- endfor %}
    <div class="siterail__foot">
      Every example runs against recorded history.
      <a class="btn btn--sm" href="/data">See the corpus</a>
      <a class="btn btn--sm btn--primary" href="/#request">Request access</a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <div class="siterail__body">
    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--ink-faint); margin-bottom: 12px">
      <a href="/use-cases/play" style="color: var(--ink-faint)">Use cases</a><span>/</span><span style="color: var(--ink-body)">{{ group.group }}</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="hero-title" style="margin-bottom: 6px">{{ group.group }}</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="margin: 0 0 8px; max-width: 62ch">
      What people actually ask their agent, and what it reads to answer.
      The numbers in these exchanges are illustrative; the tools are real.
    </p>

    {%- for c in group.cases %}
    <section id="{{ c.key }}" style="margin-top: 34px; padding-top: 22px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line)">
      <h2 class="page-title" style="font-size: 24px; margin: 0 0 8px">{{ c.title }}</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin: 0 0 20px; max-width: 62ch; font-size: 16px">{{ c.lede | safe }}</p>

      <div style="display: flex; gap: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: flex-start">
        {%- if c.script %}
        <div style="flex: 1 1 460px; min-width: 300px">
          {%- set scripts = [{ key: c.key, label: c.label, tool: c.script.tool, lines: c.script.lines }] %}
          {% include "transcript.njk" %}
        </div>
        {%- endif %}

        <div style="flex: 1 1 250px; min-width: 240px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
          <section class="panel">
            <div class="panel__head">What it reads</div>
            <div class="panel__body" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
              {%- for r in c.reads %}
              <span style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink-body)">
                <span style="width: 5px; height: 5px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--accent-bright); flex: 0 0 auto; margin-top: 7px"></span>{{ r | safe }}
              </span>
              {%- endfor %}
            </div>
          </section>
          <section class="panel">
            <div class="panel__head">To set this up</div>
            <div class="panel__body" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 9px">
              {%- for step in c.setup %}
              <a class="btn" style="justify-content: space-between" href="{{ step | setupHref }}">{{ step | safe }} →</a>
              {%- endfor %}
            </div>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    {%- endfor %}

    <p class="footnote" style="margin: 28px 0 0; max-width: 78ch">
      Every tool named above is in <a href="/tools.json">the registry</a> and
      documented in <a href="/docs/tools">the tool reference</a>. What your agent
      can answer about YOU depends on what you track;
      <a href="/docs/recording">how recording works</a> explains the difference.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<script src="/assets/transcript.js" defer></script>
